# Presentation-golden corpus manifest for Spyro 3 (fields as in
# games/spyro-1/corpus/presentation-corpus.manifest: name|start|interval|freeze|pins).
# The level loads by VBL ~1414 under --skip-to-level and gameplay is live by
# ~1773; 2073 leaves the fade settled.
# The pin holds VBL 2073 on the sub-tick leg as well as the canonical one: the
# grid's intermediate samples land at +interval/2, so the pose the player walk
# was measured against had no __inter__ tile of its own.
# 3133 pins the camera inside the portal (VBLs 3117-3162), where the
# destination's preview picture fills the screen.
# 3273 pins the level transition past the grid's last sample: the movie's
# inputs end at 3162 and the run continues, so the sub-tick leg there is
# the transition gamestate, where the re-extract draws the cyclorama and the
# player and every other producer returns empty. The grid's own 3223
# intermediate sample covers the transition's start; 3273 covers it 50 VBLs
# further in, where the canonical frame no longer moves between ticks.
# 2239: Bianca's trail effect blends toward dark where the PSX blends toward
# light; blessed pre-fix.
sunrise-spring-sunny-villa-portal-entry|2073|100||2073,2239,3133,3273

# sunrise-spring-surface-swim arms the player draw's water-plane split.
# g_Spyro+0x28 is zero on every frame of the other three bk2s and of the whole
# 20k attract demo (six levels); it is non-zero from VBL 2462 to this movie's
# end, with animationState 0x2B (SWIM_MOVE_SURFACE) and movementState 0x0A
# (SWIM_SURFACE), so the split's classification, its depth cue and its cut have
# no other row in the corpus.
sunrise-spring-surface-swim|2473|150||2473,2573,2773
# sunrise-spring-surface-swim@heldfade: a present of the held-fade loop after
# the loading screen (isbg=0, one subtractive quad per VBL over the held picture).
sunrise-spring-surface-swim@heldfade|1554|100|freeze|1556
# sunrise-spring-surface-swim@entry: the level-entry loading screen, where the
# game keeps its picture in VRAM (isbg=0) and draws only the progress strip.
# No freeze field: the headless capture keeps the retained backdrop on its own.
sunrise-spring-surface-swim@entry|1500|100||1500

# icy-peak-reflective-mirror arms the player draw's mirrored copy.
# g_Spyro+0x2C is the avatar's height above a material-class-4 surface; of the
# 37 levels only Icy Peak, Midday Gardens, Frozen Altars and Bugbot Factory
# carry a class-4 material at all, and the word is zero on every frame of the
# other four bk2s and of the whole 20k attract demo. Icy Peak spawns beside
# such a surface: idle to VBL 1873, then Up + Circle (charge) with a 60-frame
# Right every 400 to hold the rink, and the word is non-zero from VBL 2431 to
# this movie's end, so the reflection's matrix negation, its inverted
# back-face test and its ordering bias have no other row in the corpus. The
# pins are the frames where the copy is least occluded by the surface above
# it: 5011 to 7167 pixels of the frame move when the reflection is suppressed,
# against 588 to 1421 on the grid samples after 2598.
icy-peak-reflective-mirror|2473|150||2473,2494,2523,2534,2573,2574
# icy-peak-reflective-mirror@1856: the same movie at the tick that shows
# Spyro's reflection on the ice (VBL 2429), before the row above starts; the
# player colour-block swap is measured here.
icy-peak-reflective-mirror@1856|2429|600||2429
# icy-peak-reflective-mirror@1864: the same movie where the player shadow fan,
# cast onto the reflective floor's plane, lands on the ice ramp that stands
# above that plane; the decal's raised-occluder test is measured here.
icy-peak-reflective-mirror@1864|2437|600||2437,2443
# icy-peak-reflective-mirror@wall: Spyro's mirrored copy in front of the
# reflected ice wall; native drew only the tail tip, the copy pushed
# behind the reflected wall in depth. Blessed pre-fix.
icy-peak-reflective-mirror@wall|2703|600||2703
# an-evil-plot-unfolds-egg-edge: the opening cutscene under 16:9; animated-kind
# mobys inside the cull's distance box that fail its 4:3 lateral arm get no
# widened-view re-admission, so two eggs are absent from the right band at 1779
# and 1783. The left egg's disappearance between 1781 and 1782 is the game
# moving it (its 4:3 staging, kept).
an-evil-plot-unfolds-egg-edge|1773|10||1773,1779,1783,1793|--skip-to-cutscene an_evil_plot_unfolds
# a-powerful-villain-emerges-throne: the throne record switches clip at VBL 5641
# after a static span; the interp store's dedupe stretches its pair across the
# span, the COUNTSW hold re-derives the previous pose from a header the game
# has rewritten, and the throne vanishes on intermediate presents 5643-5731.
a-powerful-villain-emerges-throne|5653|10||5667|--skip-to-cutscene a_powerful_villain_emerges
# no-hard-feelings-sheila-portal: the Sheila's Alp portal (record level 16)
# opens in this cutscene; its picture is baked from Sunny Villa's sky, not its
# destination's, so the destination-sky extension leaves the 16:9 left band
# showing the flat backdrop. VBL 3304 is openpete_frame 2731 under this boot.
no-hard-feelings-sheila-portal|3304|10||3304|--skip-to-cutscene no_hard_feelings

# sunrise-spring-camera-swing holds R2 from VBL 2073 so the camera orbits the
# player while two animated-kind mobys and the simple-kind gems, baskets and
# chest stay in view. The pins hold sub-tick presents mid-swing, where an
# animated record replayed in the tick camera's view space is displaced from
# the interpolated camera by half a tick of rotation.
# 2333 and 2573 pin the swing's distant-band poses, where the far world is HP
# geometry under --lod extended and the sub-tick re-extract has the most to
# lose. They cover the pose, not the sector-occlusion class itself: the
# occluder depth grid is a GPU readback and headless holds none, so a headless
# tile cannot see a cull verdict change. That class is measured windowed, per
# walk.
# 2329 (lod extended canonical): the terrain feed of the world draw used the
# previous tick's portal openings while this tick's portal pass captured a
# different set; a sliver shows through the arch edge. Blessed pre-fix.
sunrise-spring-camera-swing|2073|100||2091,2092,2093,2113,2133,2329,2333,2573

# 2073 pins the opening dialogue, complete and static from 2067: a large
# semi-transparent text box whose corners are semi-transparent textured quads.
# sheilas-alp-sheila-water-invisible: Sheila, the playable moby, turns invisible
# in the water at VBL 5129; that pin holds the present on both legs. The 5093 pin
# holds a sub-tick present while she moves through the world under a moving
# camera: her own motion must interpolate as her camera-relative motion does.
# 5067, 5071, 5081, 5085 and 5101 hold sub-tick presents while Sheila and the
# NPCs beside her blend into their next animations.
sheilas-alp-sheila-water-invisible|4973|100||2073,5067,5071,5081,5085,5093,5101,5129

# icy-peak-ice-crystal-destruction: an ice crystal shot at VBL ~2243 shatters on the
# PSX and its model stays on screen natively; the pins bracket the shatter.
icy-peak-ice-crystal-destruction|2073|100||2233,2247,2263
# title-demo: the plain boot with no movie; the title screen's rhynoc animates
# under a fixed camera. 1083 pins the frame the jitter was reported at, on the
# canonical and the sub-tick leg alike. 2783 pins the present where particles
# streak on the intermediate leg: a primitive lerped from a previous-tick
# record that is not its own.
title-demo|1073|20||1083,2783
# title-demo-early: the title screen at VBL 663 (user report 2026-10-08):
# terrain polys of the left building missing, the purple clear colour shows
# through. Blessed pre-fix.
title-demo-early|633|20||663

# open-options and open-atlas are the corpus rows for the 2D UI layer: they are
# the only movies whose frames carry its classes inside the visible band. At
# the pins open-options draws the options panel (3 semi-transparent POLY_F4,
# PSX box x 192..320 y 76..172), its 30 SPRT glyphs (x 208..308 y 80..152) and
# 5 HUD-class POLY_FT4 (x 128..384 y 65..193); open-atlas draws the whole atlas
# screen as 290 POLY_FT4 covering x 1..512 y 12..228. The in-game HUD sprites
# sit at y -28..2 - retracted above the visible band - on every frame of every
# other movie in this corpus, so no row shows the HUD extended yet.
# Both rows are freeze-marked. From VBL 1442 the loading screen suppresses the
# framebuffer clear, and from VBL 1738 so does open-options' save prompt: the
# game draws no world and the last rendered frame is the backdrop of the 1473
# pin on both movies and of open-options 1773 and 1873. That backdrop comes
# from the capture-time snapshot, which only a freeze-marked row maintains.
# open-atlas 1573, 1773 and 1873 sit on cleared frames and are byte-identical
# with the flag and without it.
# The atlas pages at 1773 and 1873 hold vertical seams between the page's
# POLY_FT4 tiles (a black column at 16:9 x 163 and fainter ones about 52 px
# apart, each ending in a black dot) that the PSX does not draw.
# 1815: a blurred centered rectangle around the options panel outside its
# semi-transparent box, and the box corners darker than the box; PsyCross
# shows the same, the PSX does not. Blessed pre-fix.
open-options|1473|100|freeze|1773,1815,1873
# open-options@terrain: the same window under --render-paths terrain,ui; the
# window composes the copied scene, whose textures and CLUTs lie in the page
# the copy overwrites. Blessed pre-fix.
open-options@terrain|1473|100|freeze|1815|--render-paths terrain,ui
# open-atlas 1873: the guest draws Sparx over the atlas page beside the
# highlighted world; native draws the page with no Sparx. Blessed pre-fix.
open-atlas|1473|100|freeze|1773,1873

# open-atlas-turn-pages holds the atlas page-turn animation: the turning
# sheet is a skewed per-vertex-shaded quad (POLY_GT4) covering up to half the
# screen for 8 to 17 drawn ticks per turn, the only POLY_GT4 in the corpus.
# The pins bracket four turns: 1817/1825/1841/1849 (forward 1),
# 1893/1901/1917/1925 (forward 2), 2073/2083 (reverse 1) and 2097/2105
# (reverse 2), each a turning tick where the sheet covers the most screen.
open-atlas-turn-pages|1813|100|freeze|1817,1825,1841,1849,1893,1901,1917,1925,2073,2083,2097,2105

# title-demo-tracers: the attract demo's tracer ribbons, the only geometry the
# ribbon producer (func_8002FB68) emits anywhere in the corpus (VBL 5060-5108).
title-demo-tracers|5053|20||5074

# title-demo-zap: the attract demo's jittered beams, the only geometry the
# ribbon producer (func_8002F5B4) emits anywhere in the corpus: the live byte
# at +0x1C of the eight records of D_80072430 reads zero on all six gameplay
# rows and on open-atlas, and one live record on the plain boot from VBL 5474
# to VBL 5495. The 5473 grid sample sits before that window, so the row carries
# its own negative.
title-demo-zap|5473|10||5483
#
# crystal-islands-flame: a flame breath over the water in Crystal Islands with
# the HUD fully extended. The flame's primitives are written at VBL 1639-1663
# (peak 1651); 1653 is an intermediate leg inside the breath.
crystal-islands-flame|1633|200||1647,1651,1653,1659

# spikes-arena: the fight with Spike opens at ~VBL 4673. From 4693 the guest
# draws the boss health bar at the bottom right, a green-to-red gradient
# beside the boss icon; the pins 4713 and 4731 hold it on both legs.
spikes-arena|4673|100||4713,4731

# title-demo-camcut: the attract demo's third segment ends at VBL 6425 with the
# camera stepping 76110 world units in one tick, and every record the tick drew
# carries a previous tick of its own. The intermediate leg there shows the
# previous tick for the whole interval; the canonical leg is unaffected. Its own
# row rather than a pin on title-demo, whose 20-VBL grid would otherwise fan out
# over the 3600 VBLs between them.
title-demo-camcut|6373|100||6425
# title-demo-hold-player / -particles: held presents on attract-demo camera
# cuts with the player (7703-7704) and particles (11052-11053) on screen; a
# held cut draws tick N-1's sets under tick N-1's camera. Blessed pre-fix.
# -particles is freeze-marked: at its 10973 sample the game is in gamestate 5
# with DRAWENV isbg=0, retaining the last rendered frame, which only the
# capture-time snapshot maintains; 11052, 11053 and 11073 are byte-identical
# with the flag and without it.
title-demo-hold-player|7673|100||7703,7704
title-demo-hold-particles|10973|100|freeze|11052,11053
# title-demo-segment-fade / -2: attract-demo segment changes, where the
# loading image fades in on ticks with no 3D producer; the canonical present
# drew the previous presented scene and its fade. Blessed pre-fix.
title-demo-segment-fade|3573|100||3669,3673,3697
title-demo-segment-fade-2|15073|100||15094
# sunny-villa @heldfx: held presents where glint and tracers drew tick N's
# set (or none) instead of tick N-1's. Blessed pre-fix.
sunrise-spring-sunny-villa-portal-entry@heldfx|2473|100||2500,3004,3066
# the_second_warning cutscene, VBL 1866-1874: Bianca interpolates wrongly on
# the sub-tick view just before she steps out from behind the tree (native).
second-warning-bianca-tree|1862|2||1866,1868,1870,1871,1872,1873,1874|--skip-to-cutscene the_second_warning
# the_second_warning cutscene, VBL 2358-2366: Hunter interpolates wrongly on
# the sub-tick view (native).
second-warning-hunter|2354|2||2358,2360,2361,2362,2363,2364,2366|--skip-to-cutscene the_second_warning
# attract-projectile-jump: class 0x1a2 copies a source moby's position into
# a hidden record on state 30 -> 4 (a placement). Blessed pre-fix.
attract-projectile-jump|4997|2||4999,5000,5001,5002,5003
# second-warning-hunter-cut: an authored camera cut at VBL 1924 while Hunter
# steps one 1639-unit sampler key; the held cut keeps the camera at tick N-1
# while his record interpolated. Blessed pre-fix.
second-warning-hunter-cut|1920|2||1922,1923,1924,1925,1926|--skip-to-cutscene the_second_warning
# second-warning-held-particles: held camera cuts at VBL 2372 and 2636 where
# tick N-1 drew particles and tick N captured none, and 2562 where tick N-1
# captured none; a held present draws exactly tick N-1's set. Blessed pre-fix.
second-warning-held-particles|2372|264||2372,2562,2636|--skip-to-cutscene the_second_warning

# cloud-spires-game-over: the game-over reload. The game-over image is read
# through the synchronous reader with loadStage already 2; deferring that
# read's completion hangs the reader's no-VSync spin (watchdog exit at VBL
# 5916). 5973 is the game-over screen, 7873 the reloaded level live.
cloud-spires-game-over|5973|1000||5973,7873
#
# s3-create-save: a new game on a blank card in slot 1 (provisioned formatted
# by the binary in the leg's directory) creates and writes its save. 1678 and
# 2341 are presents where the game draws nothing: the display shows the last
# image drawn into the buffer it shows, the world under the card dialogue.
s3-create-save|1678|663||1678,2341|--card1 {legdir}/card1.mcr --no-card2

# spooky-swamp-area-1-respawn-clear: the respawn fade (game.state 3) ends at
# a subtraction of 240, then each tick DrawOTags an empty OT into a buffer
# whose DRAWENV auto-clears to black. 2900 and 3000 show the cleared buffer,
# where the area's last scene showed under its kept fade before.
spooky-swamp-area-1-respawn-clear|2900|100||2900,3000

# credits-cheat: the pause-menu credits cheat from Sunrise Spring. The credits
# overlay emits one subtractive full-width quad of grey D_8006C598 << 4 per
# tick while D_8006C598 != 0: the fade-in from black at VBL 2013-2043 and the
# fade through black at each scene change (3695-3757). 2025, 3708 and 3720
# are fade presents; 3690 precedes the fade. 2256 and 2600 are sub-tick
# presents with credits letters flying in and departing: the draw compacts
# the CreditsLetter records in states 1-3 into consecutive moby slots, so a
# departing or reused record moves every later letter to another slot.
credits-cheat|2013|200||2025,2256,2600,3690,3708,3720
#
# sunny-villa-level-entry: the level entry from Sunrise Spring into Sunny
# Villa, ending on the loading screen's treasure tally (VBL ~4240-4720; the
# gems fly 4320-4470). The movie ends at 3949 and the row samples the game
# running on without input. In builder state 3 (D_8006FBC8) the loading
# overlay rebuilds the moby array every tick: one class-1 moby per active
# tally record (*D_8006C764, stride 8, active byte +4), then the counter gem
# (+0x0C 0x154, +0x14 0xC00), then the total gem (+0x0C 0xB4). 4370 and 4430
# are sub-tick presents with gems in flight: a spawn or a landing moves every
# later gem to another slot.
sunny-villa-level-entry|4300|200||4370,4430
# Cutscene letterbox bars growing 2 PSX rows per tick (VBL 1605-1627): the
# intermediate leg must show them between the two ticks. Blessed pre-fix.
agent_9s_lab-letterbox|1605|2||1607,1617|--skip-to-level agent_9s_lab
